# Note: the ruleset on `main` deliberately does NOT require code-owner
# approval. GitHub does not let you approve your own pull request, and this is
# a single-maintainer repository — requiring it would make every PR
# unmergeable, including this file's own. CODEOWNERS earns its keep here by
# routing review on agent-authored PRs, which are opened by a bot and so *can*
# be approved by the owner.
